  "inference": "The original DEX has no exception handlers in the app listener. On every normal return after a positive network test it reads the current app account and calls the controller method ci(GmailAndroidAccount). Taken together, the observed network result and normal return place both full pulls through this account-specific call. The concrete work it selected was not observed.",
  "interpretation": "On the board, four full pulls across two observation builds reached the original Gmail refresh listener and returned. Two short pulls took the cancel animation. In the enhanced build, both full pulls received a non-null active Android network and isConnected returned true on the Gmail listener stack. No monitored Android provider method ran directly on that stack and no new local mailbox sync or token request was observed. Delivery of the new email and Gmail’s asynchronous work after the listener remain open.",
